STAAD SPACE SENTRY POST - RC MOMENT FRAME WITH BALLISTIC INFILL
*
* ==========================================================================
*  SENTRY POST - UNDERGROUND CBRN SHELTER COMPLEX, PUNE
*  FRAMED SCHEME.  Supersedes the load-bearing wall model for design of the
*  frame members.  Same building, same levels, different lateral system.
*
*  FRAME     4 corner columns + 4 beams per level, 2 storeys
*  GRID      3.650 (X) x 4.650 (Z) centre to centre of columns
*            column outer faces flush with the 4.000 x 5.000
*            external faces, so they project inward only
*  COLUMNS   350 x 350 square
*  BEAMS     250 wide x 450 deep, all beams both levels
*  SLAB      150 two-way, load shed to the beams by 45 deg lines
*  INFILL    200 RC ballistic panels, NON structural - carried by
*            the beam at the foot of each storey as a UDL
*  LEVELS    base +0.450   first floor +3.650   roof +6.700
*  MATERIAL  M30 / Fe500,  Ec = 27.386 x 10^6 kN/m2
*  SIZE      12 joints, 16 members, 4 fixed supports
*
* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  SEISMIC BASIS - IS 1893 (Part 1) : 2016
* --------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Pune, Zone III                 Z = 0.16    Table 3
*  Defence installation           I = 1.5     Table 8, critical/lifeline
*  Response reduction             R = 3.0     Table 9 - SEE THE NOTE BELOW
*
*  WHY R = 3.0 AND NOT 5.0.  The four faces carry 200 mm RC ballistic
*  panels.  Unless every panel is positively separated from the frame, they
*  are far stiffer than the columns and the building resists the earthquake
*  as a WALL system, not as a special moment frame.  R = 3.0 is therefore
*  adopted, the same value as the wall scheme, and the frame members are
*  designed for the whole of that base shear - a conservative lower bound.
*  If the panels are isolated from the frame and IS 13920 SMRF detailing is
*  provided, R = 5.0 applies and every seismic force here scales by 3/5
*  (VB would fall from 73.18 kN to 43.91 kN).
*
*  Cl 7.6.2   Ta = 0.09 h / sqrt(d)  for buildings with infills
*             h = 6.250 m
*             X:  d = 4.000  ->  Ta = 0.2812 s
*             Z:  d = 5.000  ->  Ta = 0.2516 s
*             bare RC MRF, 0.075 h^0.75, would give 0.2965 s
*             all three lie inside 0.10 - 0.40 s where Sa/g = 2.50 for
*             soil types I, II and III alike, so neither the soil class nor
*             the choice of period formula changes the base shear.
*
*  Cl 6.4.2   Ah = (Z/2)(Sa/g)(I/R)
*                = (0.16/2)(2.50)(1.5/3.0) = 0.1000
*
*  SEISMIC WEIGHT   Cl 7.3.1, 7.3.2 and Table 10
*     roof   +6.700    W2 =   331.46 kN
*     floor  +3.650    W1 =   400.34 kN
*                      W  =   731.80 kN
*  Cl 7.6.1   VB = Ah W = 0.1000 x 731.80 = 73.18 kN
*  Cl 7.6.3   Qi = VB Wi hi^2 / SUM( Wj hj^2 )
*     Q2 =  55.58 kN at +6.700 -> 13.8954 kN at each of 4 joints
*     Q1 =  17.60 kN at +3.650 -> 4.3996 kN at each of 4 joints
*
*  CARRIED BY THE PLINTH BEAM, NOT BY THIS FRAME:
*     ground storey infill 13.750 kN/m over 16.600 m = 228.25 kN
*     design the 250 x 400 plinth beam and the
*     footings separately from the support reactions.  The weight IS
*     included in W1 above, per Cl 7.3.1.
*
*  NOT MODELLED: openings in the infill (conservative for load); accidental
*  torsion, Cl 7.8.2 - add +/- 0.05 b; the external spiral stair.
*  Units: metre, kilonewton.  Y is vertical.
* ==========================================================================
*
START JOB INFORMATION
ENGINEER DATE 24-Aug-2026
JOB NAME SENTRY POST - FRAMED - SEISMIC
END JOB INFORMATION
*
INPUT WIDTH 79
UNIT METER KN
JOINT COORDINATES
1 0.175 0.45 0.175; 2 0.175 0.45 4.825; 11 3.825 0.45 0.175;
12 3.825 0.45 4.825; 101 0.175 3.65 0.175; 102 0.175 3.65 4.825;
111 3.825 3.65 0.175; 112 3.825 3.65 4.825; 201 0.175 6.7 0.175;
202 0.175 6.7 4.825; 211 3.825 6.7 0.175; 212 3.825 6.7 4.825;
*
MEMBER INCIDENCES
1 1 101; 2 2 102; 3 11 111; 4 12 112; 5 101 201; 6 102 202; 7 111 211;
8 112 212; 9 101 111; 10 102 112; 11 101 102; 12 111 112; 13 201 211;
14 202 212; 15 201 202; 16 211 212;
*
START GROUP DEFINITION
MEMBER
_COL_GF 1 TO 4
_COL_FF 5 TO 8
_BEAM_FF 9 TO 12
_BEAM_RF 13 TO 16
END GROUP DEFINITION
*
DEFINE MATERIAL START
ISOTROPIC M30
E 2.73861e+07
POISSON 0.2
DENSITY 25
ALPHA 1e-05
DAMP 0.05
TYPE CONCRETE
STRENGTH FCU 30000
END DEFINE MATERIAL
*
MEMBER PROPERTY
* columns 350 square - square, so the BETA angle cannot matter
1 TO 8 PRIS YD 0.35 ZD 0.35
* beams 250 x 450, YD is the depth
9 TO 16 PRIS YD 0.45 ZD 0.25
*
CONSTANTS
MATERIAL M30 ALL
*
SUPPORTS
1 2 11 12 FIXED
*
* ============================ LOADING =====================================
LOAD 1 LOADTYPE Dead  TITLE DL SELFWEIGHT SLAB INFILL PARAPET
SELFWEIGHT Y -1 
MEMBER LOAD
